Broker constraints come next. The stop must lie on the correct side of the current price and at least SYMBOL_TRADE_STOPS_LEVEL points away from it. An existing SL or TP that is closer to the price than SYMBOL_TRADE_FREEZE_LEVEL points cannot be modified, so the modification is rejected. Both levels are read in points and converted to price units with SYMBOL_POINT. For a partial close, the validator checks that both the closed volume and the remaining volume are multiples of the volume step and inside the broker volume range (lots). For a full close, it takes the volume from the freshly read position.
The engine does not implement an exposure guard. It never opens or adds to positions; every action either reduces volume or moves a stop, so an exposure limit would never apply.
Execution Adapter
The execution adapter is the only component that sends orders. It converts a validated SExitAdjustment into an MqlTradeRequest. For full and partial closes it uses TRADE_ACTION_DEAL with the opposite order type (sell to close a buy, buy to close a sell), the current bid or ask, a configurable deviation (points), and a filling mode supported by the symbol. For stop modifications it uses TRADE_ACTION_SLTP.
